      "englishLanguage": {"status":"unverified","note":"Not verified: University of Oxford’s pages could not be opened for checking on 19 Oct 2026 — check the official page.","reviewFlag":"Re-check in a browser: https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate/applying-to-oxford/for-international-students/ELR (HTTP 403 to automated checks on 2026-10-19). Record the English language requirement (IELTS overall and per component, TOEFL and other tests; standard or higher level) for this course, with a verbatim snippet."},
      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.history.ox.ac.uk/making-application","label":"Oxford History: Making an application"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Applicants for History, Ancient and Modern History, History and English, and History and Modern Languages do not take an admissions test"],"note":"The same page still mentions “the HAT” in its subject advice — older wording; the current statement is that History applicants take no admissions test."},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["No required subjects","History strongly advised (not an absolute requirement); other subjects do not matter"],"codes":["History","English"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.history.ox.ac.uk/making-application","label":"Oxford History: Making an application"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["You are strongly advised to take history as one of your subjects, but it is not an absolute requirement. … As long as you have sufficient history experience, it really doesn’t matter what other subjects you take."],"note":"English is not mentioned by the History Faculty for single-honours History; it is kept as a preferred code from the course dataset. Partly verified: the official page states History is strongly advised but does not name English, which is held as preferred for matching.","reviewFlag":"Official page strongly advises History but does not name English; data/courseRequirements.js holds preferred [History, English]. Owner decision."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"partial","accepted":"yes","typicalOffer":"AAA","subjects":{"preferred":[{"name":"History","code":"History"},{"name":"English Literature (or English Language and Literature)","code":"English"}]},"sources":[{"url":"https://www.history.ox.ac.uk/making-application","label":"Oxford History: Making an application"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["The offer for all history courses is: 3 As at A Level … You are strongly advised to take history as one of your subjects, but it is not an absolute requirement. … As long as you have sufficient history experience, it really doesn’t matter what other subjects you take."],"note":"History is strongly advised but not an absolute requirement; English is not mentioned for single-honours History (kept as preferred from the course dataset). Partly verified: the official page states History is strongly advised but does not name English, which is held as preferred for matching.","reviewFlag":"Official page strongly advises History but does not name English; data/courseRequirements.js holds preferred [History, English]. Owner decision."},
      "ib": {"status":"partial","accepted":"yes","overallScore":38,"detail":"666 at HL","subjects":{"preferred":[{"name":"History","code":"History"},{"name":"English A","code":"English"}]},"coreNote":"38 points includes core points","sources":[{"url":"https://www.history.ox.ac.uk/making-application","label":"Oxford History: Making an application"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["38 at International Baccalaureate (including core points) with 666 at HL"],"note":"Partly verified: the official page states History is strongly advised but does not name English, which is held as preferred for matching.","reviewFlag":"Official page strongly advises History but does not name English; data/courseRequirements.js holds preferred [History, English]. Owner decision."},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"unverified","note":"Not verified: University of Oxford’s pages could not be opened for checking on 19 Oct 2026 — check the official page.","reviewFlag":"Re-check in a browser: https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate/applying-to-oxford/for-international-students/international-qualifications (HTTP 403 to automated checks on 2026-10-19). Record the AP requirement for applicants with a US high-school diploma for this course, with a verbatim snippet."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"partial","items":["Written work: a piece of historical writing with a signed cover sheet","Interviews for shortlisted applicants (online); some colleges set a short passage to read before interview"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.history.ox.ac.uk/making-application","label":"Oxford History: Making an application"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["We use your written work to help assess your reasoning, language and writing skills. … The work must be accompanied by a cover sheet, that is also signed by a member of staff at your school/college … The interview is designed to assess your academic potential. … Following a university-wide vote, all interviews will be on-line. … Some colleges may require you to read a short passage of historical writing just before your interview, which they will ask you to discuss as part of the interview process."],"note":"The interview dates on this page (weeks of 9 and 16 December) appear to be from an earlier cycle. Partly verified: the page still shows details from an earlier admissions cycle."}
