      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Interview days: the department plans to hold them as part of selection; details not yet published","ATAS certificate needed for the visa unless your nationality is exempt (US, EEA and others are exempt)","Year-abroad variants: ability in the relevant language, usually GCSE grade A or an AS-level pass"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.imperial.ac.uk/study/courses/undergraduate/chemical-engineering/","label":"Imperial: Chemical Engineering MEng"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"The Department plans to hold interview days as part of the selection process. Check back soon for more information. … Unless you are from an exempt nationality, you will need an ATAS certificate to obtain your visa and study this course. … Grade A in GCSE or a pass at AS-level will usually be required."}
