      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","items":["TMUA — required if you apply on or before the last TMUA booking deadline","Applicants who apply after that deadline and cannot sit the TMUA will typically have at least one STEP paper in their conditional offer","The MAT is no longer used by Imperial"],"codes":["TMUA"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.imperial.ac.uk/study/courses/undergraduate/mathematics-bsc/","label":"Imperial: Mathematics BSc"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If you submit your application to Imperial on or before the last TMUA booking deadline, you are required to take the TMUA. We expect most of our offers to go to applicants who have taken the TMUA. For candidates who apply after the last TMUA booking deadline, and are unable to sit the TMUA, conditional offers will typically require you to sit at least one Sixth Term Examination Paper (STEP)."},
