      "satAct": {"status":"verified","items":["For applicants with a US high-school diploma (the diploma alone is not sufficient): one accepted route for A*AA/AAA offers is a minimum High School Diploma GPA of 3.7 plus ACT 32+ or SAT 1450+, with AP Calculus BC at grade 5 because this programme requires Mathematics","SAT/ACT is not the only route: five APs at grade 5 with a GPA of 3.7 is the alternative"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.lse.ac.uk/study-at-lse/international-students/united-states-of-america","label":"LSE: United States of America (international students)"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Please note that the US High School Diploma by itself isn't sufficient for entry to LSE. … A*AA, AAA Five APs at grade 5, taken over a maximum of three years and a minimum High School Diploma GPA 3.7 (subjects may be specified as part of an offer, see the note below about subject combinations). Or a minimum High School Diploma GPA of 3.7, and an ACT score of 32+ or an SAT score of 1450+ (with AP Calculus BC at grade 5 for programmes with a Mathematics requirement)."},
      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["IELTS Academic: 7.0 overall and 7.0 in each component (one sitting)","TOEFL iBT: 100 overall with at least 27 Writing, 25 Reading, 24 Listening, 24 Speaking (updated-scale tests from January 2026: 5.5 overall, 5 in each skill)","PTE Academic (in person only): 70 overall with 70 in all components","Cambridge C1 Advanced / C2 Proficiency: 185 overall and 185 in each component","Proof is needed only if LSE makes an offer; nationals of Canada or a UKVI majority English-speaking country whose first language is English are exempt"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.lse.ac.uk/study-at-lse/Undergraduate/Prospective-Students/How-to-Apply/English-language-requirements","label":"LSE: English language requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"IELTS Academic (International English Language Testing Service) Including online version 7.0 overall and 7.0 in each component … Pearson Test of English (Academic) (PTEA) (in person only) 70 overall with 70 in all components (in one sitting) … TOEFL iBT (including Home and Paper Editions) 100 overall, with a minimum of: 27 in Writing 25 in Reading 24 in Listening 24 in Speaking"},
      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.lse.ac.uk/study-at-lse/Undergraduate/Prospective-Students/How-to-Apply/Entry-Requirements","label":"LSE: Undergraduate entry requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"For these two programmes for September 2027 entry taking the TMUA is mandatory – all applicants are required to take the test. BSc Economics BSc Econometrics and Mathematical Economics … The LNAT is not required for any other programme at LSE.","note":"LSE’s entry-requirements page lists the TMUA as mandatory only for BSc Economics and BSc Econometrics and Mathematical Economics (recommended for eight other programmes, not this one) and the LNAT only for the LLB."},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"verified","items":["Required: Mathematics (A-level or equivalent)","No set subject combination; typical choices include Government and Politics, History, English, Economics, Sociology, Philosophy, languages and Mathematics"],"codes":["Mathematics_Standard"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.lse.ac.uk/study-at-lse/undergraduate/bsc-politics-and-economics","label":"LSE: BSc Politics and Economics"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"There is no set subject combination, although A-level Mathematics (or equivalent) is required. Typical subject choices include Government and Politics, History, English, Economics, Sociology, Philosophy, languages and Mathematics."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","typicalOffer":"AAA","subjects":{"required":[{"name":"Mathematics","code":"Mathematics_Standard"}]},"sources":[{"url":"https://www.lse.ac.uk/study-at-lse/undergraduate/bsc-politics-and-economics","label":"LSE: BSc Politics and Economics"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"A-levels AAA, including Mathematics … A-level contextual offers AAB, including A in Mathematics … There is no set subject combination, although A-level Mathematics (or equivalent) is required.","note":"AAA, including Mathematics.","reviewFlag":"Contextual offer is display-only — the matcher does not apply it.","contextualOffer":"AAB, including A in Mathematics"},
