      "ib": {"status":"partial","accepted":"yes","overallScore":39,"detail":"666 at HL","subjects":{"standardLevel":[{"name":"English at 5","code":"English"},{"name":"Mathematics at 6","code":"Mathematics_Standard"}]},"contextualOffer":"34 points with 655 at HL — minimum entry requirement for widening access Plus Flag applicants (UK permanent residents only)","sources":[{"url":"https://study.ed.ac.uk/programmes/undergraduate/120-architecture/entry-requirements","label":"Edinburgh: Architecture BA/MA (Hons) entry requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"These are the range of grades most applicants needed to receive an offer in recent years: from 37 points with 666 at HL to 34 points with 655 at HL … no specific subjects required Your HLs can be in any subject. … English at 5 Mathematics at 6 Evidence of artistic ability is normally required at either HL or SL, for example Visual Arts or Design Technology.","note":"Standard entry requirement from 37 points with 666 at HL to 34 points with 655 at HL; no HL subjects required; SL English 5 and SL Mathematics 6; evidence of artistic ability normally required at HL or SL (e.g. Visual Arts or Design Technology). Edinburgh describes its standard entry requirements as the grades most applicants needed to receive an offer in recent years; offers may be made above or below them, and never below the widening-access minimum.","reviewFlag":"Edinburgh publishes 37/666 to 34/655 — 39 points (engine) is above it. Owner decision. Widening-access minimum and SL subjects are display-only."},
