      "otherRequirements": {"status":"partial","items":["No interview: Edinburgh interviews only for medicine, nursing, teacher education and veterinary medicine","Evidence of artistic ability is normally required through qualifications (A level/GCSE or IB); the 2027-entry entry-requirements page lists no portfolio or other additional requirement"],"sources":[{"url":"https://study.ed.ac.uk/undergraduate/applying/selection/interviews-tests-portfolios","label":"Edinburgh: Interviews, tests and portfolios"},{"url":"https://study.ed.ac.uk/programmes/undergraduate/120-architecture/entry-requirements","label":"Edinburgh: Architecture BA/MA (Hons) entry requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["You may be invited to an interview for degree programmes in: medicine nursing teacher education veterinary medicine For medicine and veterinary medicine this will take the form of multiple mini-interviews. We do not interview for entry to any other degree programmes. … Applicants to art, design and fine art degrees will be asked to submit a digital portfolio.","Evidence of artistic ability is normally required at either A level or GCSE."],"note":"Edinburgh asks applicants to art, design and fine art degrees for a digital portfolio; the Architecture entry-requirements page lists no portfolio, but it does not say explicitly that none is needed — check the degree finder before applying."}
