      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Required: Mathematics — A level Mathematics at A*, or IB HL Mathematics (Analysis and approaches only) at 7, achieved no more than two academic years before entry","Preferred: Further Mathematics"],"codes":["Mathematics_Standard","Mathematics_Advanced"],"sources":[{"url":"https://study.ed.ac.uk/programmes/undergraduate/55-mathematics/entry-requirements","label":"Edinburgh: Mathematics BSc (Hons) entry requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Mathematics at A* Applicants with Further Mathematics preferred.","note":"Mathematics at A* required; Further Mathematics preferred. The IB HL Mathematics 7 and two-year recency details are quoted in the A level/IB rows, not in this row's snippet.","reviewFlag":"IB and recency details in the item need quoting in this row's snippet to verify."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"partial","accepted":"yes","detail":"Standard entry requirement (range): from A*A*A* to A*AB in one set of exams, including Mathematics at A*; applicants with Further Mathematics preferred. Direct entry to Year 2 may be possible with A*A*A* including Mathematics A* and Further Mathematics A*.","subjects":{"required":[{"name":"Mathematics","code":"Mathematics_Standard"}],"excluded":[{"name":"Applied ICT","code":"Other"},{"name":"Applied Science","code":"Other"},{"name":"Communication and Culture","code":"Other"},{"name":"Creative Writing","code":"Other"},{"name":"General Studies","code":"Other"},{"name":"Journalism in the Media and Communications Industry","code":"Other"},{"name":"Leisure Studies","code":"Other"},{"name":"Media: Communication and Production","code":"Other"},{"name":"Performing Arts","code":"Drama"},{"name":"Travel and Tourism","code":"Other"}],"preferred":[{"name":"Further Mathematics","code":"Mathematics_Advanced"}]},"contextualOffer":"A*AB, including Mathematics at A* — minimum entry requirement for widening access Plus Flag applicants (UK permanent residents only)","sources":[{"url":"https://study.ed.ac.uk/programmes/undergraduate/55-mathematics/entry-requirements","label":"Edinburgh: Mathematics BSc (Hons) entry requirements"},{"url":"https://study.ed.ac.uk/undergraduate/entry-requirements/english-welsh-northern-irish-qualifications/approved-subjects","label":"Edinburgh: Approved A level subjects"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["These are the range of grades most applicants needed to receive an offer in recent years: from A*A*A* to A*AB in one set of exams … Mathematics at A* Applicants with Further Mathematics preferred. Your Mathematics qualifications must have been achieved no more than two academic years prior to entry. … A*A*A* in one set of exams to include Mathematics at A* and Further Mathematics at A* … The A level grades you need to be considered for an offer A*AB","A level subjects we do not accept Applied ICT Applied Science Communication and Culture Creative Writing General Studies Journalism in the Media and Communications Industry Leisure Studies Media: Communication and Production Performing Arts Travel and Tourism"],"note":"Standard entry requirement from A*A*A* to A*AB in one set of exams, including Mathematics at A* (no more than two academic years before entry); Further Mathematics preferred. No typical offer is shown because the matching engine stores no A-Level offer for this course (by owner policy, published ranges are not stored as offers). GCSE English at C or 4 is not in this row's snippet. Edinburgh describes its standard entry requirements as the grades most applicants needed to receive an offer in recent years; offers may be made above or below them, and never below the widening-access minimum.","reviewFlag":"The engine holds no A-Level offer (grades.aLevels null) — the published range is shown in \"detail\" only. Owner decision. The widening-access (Plus Flag) minimum offer and the excluded A level subjects are display-only; the matcher does not apply them."},
      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","subjects":{"required":[{"name":"Mathematics","code":"Mathematics_Standard"}],"higherLevel":[{"name":"Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches","code":"Mathematics_Advanced"}],"standardLevel":[{"name":"English at 5","code":"English"}],"preferred":[{"name":"Mathematics at Higher Level","code":"Mathematics_Advanced"}]},"detail":"7 in HL Mathematics (Analysis and Approaches only) is firm in any offer; SL English 5","contextualOffer":"32 points with 765 at HL — minimum entry requirement for widening access Plus Flag applicants (UK permanent residents only)","sources":[{"url":"https://study.ed.ac.uk/programmes/undergraduate/55-mathematics/entry-requirements","label":"Edinburgh: Mathematics BSc (Hons) entry requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"These are the range of grades most applicants needed to receive an offer in recent years: from 38 points with 766 at HL to 34 points with 765 at HL … Mathematics (Analysis and approaches only) at 7 … The IB grades you need to be considered for an offer 32 points with 765 at HL","note":"Edinburgh publishes a standard range from 38 points with 766 at HL to 34 points with 765 at HL (2027 entry); no IB points score is shown because the matching engine stores none for this course. HL Mathematics (Analysis and approaches only) at 7 and SL English at 5 are required; Year 2 entry may be possible with 38 points and 766 at HL. Edinburgh describes its standard entry requirements as the grades most applicants needed to receive an offer in recent years; offers may be made above or below them, and never below the widening-access minimum.","reviewFlag":"The widening-access minimum (32 points with 765 at HL) and SL English are display-only; the matcher does not apply them."},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["Advanced Placement: 3 AP exams; Not counted: AP Research","School of Mathematics: AP Calculus at 5 is required; AP Calculus BC in addition to AP Calculus AB may be preferred","AP Seminar, AP Research and AP Studio Art are not accepted for entry to College of Science and Engineering programmes","AP scores are used for admissions only; no advanced credit is awarded"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.ed.ac.uk/studying/international/country/americas/united-states-of-america","label":"Edinburgh: Undergraduate entry requirements — United States of America"},{"url":"https://science-engineering.ed.ac.uk/studying/undergraduate/applying/entrancerequirements/entry-requirements-for-usa-qualifications","label":"Edinburgh College of Science and Engineering: Applying with USA qualifications"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Please note, AP scores are used for admissions purposes only, and no advanced credit is awarded as there is no core curriculum in Scotland. AP Research is not accepted as meeting one of the three minimum standardised test scores required.","Required subjects for programmes in the School of Mathematics: AP calculus at 5. For Mathematics and Music: AP calculus and Music is recommended. For Mathematics and Physics: AP calculus at 5 and Physics. Applicants with AP Calculus BC in addition to AP Calculus AB may be preferred. … we do not accept AP Seminar, AP Research or AP Studio Art for entry purposes;"]},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"partial","items":["No interview: Edinburgh interviews only for medicine, nursing, teacher education and veterinary medicine","No portfolio or other additional requirement is listed for this programme"],"sources":[{"url":"https://study.ed.ac.uk/undergraduate/applying/selection/interviews-tests-portfolios","label":"Edinburgh: Interviews, tests and portfolios"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"You may be invited to an interview for degree programmes in: medicine nursing teacher education veterinary medicine For medicine and veterinary medicine this will take the form of multiple mini-interviews. We do not interview for entry to any other degree programmes.","note":"Partly verified: Edinburgh’s interviews, tests and portfolios page still refers to the UCAT “in 2025” (the previous cycle)."}
