      "otherQualifications": {"status":"partial","items":["Advanced Placement: 3 AP exams at grades 4, 4, 4; Minimum GPA 3.2","Official: US high-school diploma with GPA 3.2 minimum (3.4 for competitive courses) plus three additional qualifications — AP tests at 4 or above (more commonly 5), AP classes over two semesters, Honors classes, dual-enrolment courses, SAT/ACT, IB Higher Level courses or A levels"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.bristol.ac.uk/international/countries/usa.html","label":"Bristol: USA – entry requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"We will consider applicants with a high school diploma (or equivalent) with a GPA of 3.2 minimum (3.4 for competitive courses) and three additional qualifications, which can be any of the following: SAT (evidence-based reading and writing section only) with a minimum of 650 or ACT with a minimum score of 28 AP Tests with a score of at least 4 (more commonly 5)","note":"Official (2027 entry): high-school diploma with GPA 3.2 minimum (3.4 for competitive courses) and three additional qualifications; AP tests count at a score of at least 4 (more commonly 5). Bristol does not say which courses count as competitive, and APs are one of several qualification types that can make up the three.","reviewFlag":"Bristol’s USA page sets GPA 3.2 minimum (3.4 for competitive courses) plus three additional qualifications, with APs at 4+ (more commonly 5); data/courseRequirements.js holds \"Advanced Placement: 3 AP exams at grades 4, 4, 4; Minimum GPA 3.2\". Owner decision."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Applications are assessed on academic record (GCSE and A-level or equivalent) together with the LNAT score","LNAT essay: Bristol looks for the ability to make and sustain a persuasive argument and a strong command of language","Personal statement and reference are not normally considered — used only to separate applicants with the same academic score","Not routinely interviewed (interviews only in exceptional circumstances)"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.bristol.ac.uk/study/media/undergraduate/admissions-statements/2027/law.pdf","label":"Bristol: Admissions Statement 2027 – Law"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"When considering an application, we take into account the applicant's academic record, ie. their GCSE results (or equivalent) and achieved or predicted results in A-Levels (or equivalent), as well as the applicant's LNAT score. … Within the essay section, we look for candidates who can demonstrate the ability to make and sustain a persuasive argument and have a strong command of language. … We do not normally consider the personal statement and reference. … For these courses, applicants are not routinely interviewed."}
