      "otherQualifications": {"status":"partial","items":["Advanced Placement: 2 AP exams","Official (A*AA course): three AP exams at 5, 5, 5, or two AP exams at 5, 5 plus one of SAT/ACT, an honours course or a year-long dual-enrolment course","A required A-level Mathematics must be shown by AP Calculus BC at grade 5","AP exams must be sat and submitted — the AP course grade is not accepted; AP Capstone (AP Research, AP Seminar) does not count"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.durham.ac.uk/business/courses/economics-l100/","label":"Durham: Economics L100 (September 2027)"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If your school offers AP curriculum, you will need to submit a minimum of two AP exam scores in order to meet the academic entry requirements for your degree programme of choice. … A*AA Three AP test scores of: 5,5,5 Two AP test scores of: 5,5 PLUS one of the following: SAT I: 1350 (min 700 RW, 650 M) ACT: 30","note":"Official (2027 entry): for a A*AA course, three AP exams at 5, 5, 5, or two AP exams at 5, 5 plus one additional qualification (SAT, ACT, honours course or dual-enrolment course). Two AP exams alone do not meet the requirement. Students at schools without AP may use honours courses with an overall GPA of 3.7.","reviewFlag":"Durham’s course page requires three APs at 5,5,5 or two APs at 5,5 plus a third qualification for a A*AA course; data/courseRequirements.js holds \"Advanced Placement: 2 AP exams\". Owner decision."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Selection uses achieved and predicted qualifications, the personal statement and reference(s)","Interviews or written work: the policy says some courses require them, with details on the course page; the 2027 course page does not mention either"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.durham.ac.uk/media/durham-university/study/admissions-policies/Admissions-Policy-2026-27.pdf","label":"Durham: Admissions Policy 2026/27"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Personal statements are given consideration alongside other listed criteria. … In addition, some courses may require applicants to participate in an interview, submit examples of written work, compositions, or sound/video files of performance as part of the selection process. Further information is provided on relevant course pages."}
