      "otherQualifications": {"status":"partial","items":["Advanced Placement (US applicants, university-wide minimum): three approved AP exams ranging from 5,5,5 to 4,4,4 (or Honors / college-level / dual-enrolment classes, or a combination of three distinct ones); subject preferences may apply and many courses ask for more"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/studywithus/international-applicants/country-info/countryinformation/usa.aspx","label":"Nottingham: USA – country information"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Entry requirements to our bachelors degree programmes vary depending on your chosen course, however as a minimum requirement, you will typically need one of the following: 3 approved AP Exams ranging between 5, 5, 5 to 4, 4, 4 3 Honors classes ranging between A+, A, A to B+, B+, B+ 3 College Level/Dual Enrolment classes ranging between A+, A, A to B+, B+, B+ … Subject preferences may apply, please get in touch for individual queries. Many courses will have higher requirements than the minimum listed above.","note":"Nottingham publishes only a university-wide range for AP; the Economics page points to the country page and states no course-specific AP grades or subjects."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Selection on the academic record and the whole UCAS application: academic reference and personal statement"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/studywithus/ugstudy/courses/UG/Economics-BSc-Hons.html","label":"Nottingham: Economics BSc (Hons) (2027 entry)"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Selection of those applicants will be based upon a combination of the candidate's academic record and an assessment of all the information provided in their UCAS application, their academic reference and their personal statement.","note":"No interview or admissions test is described on the 2027 course page."}
