      "satAct": {"status":"verified","items":["For applicants with US high-school qualifications: Nottingham does not generally require standardised tests (SAT/ACT); medical applicants must take the UCAT (the page still calls it the UKCAT)","Minimum academic route: three approved AP exams (5,5,5 to 4,4,4), three Honors classes, three college-level/dual-enrolment classes, or a combination of three distinct ones — many courses ask for more"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/studywithus/international-applicants/country-info/countryinformation/usa.aspx","label":"Nottingham: USA – country information"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Entry requirements to our bachelors degree programmes vary depending on your chosen course, however as a minimum requirement, you will typically need one of the following: 3 approved AP Exams ranging between 5, 5, 5 to 4, 4, 4 3 Honors classes ranging between A+, A, A to B+, B+, B+ 3 College Level/Dual Enrolment classes ranging between A+, A, A to B+, B+, B+ … We do not generally require any standardised tests, but medical applicants are required to take the UKCAT test.","note":"University-wide guidance on Nottingham’s USA country page (undated); it uses the old UKCAT name and quotes an older range of A-level/IB offers, so it may not have been updated recently."},
      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["IELTS: 6.5 overall, no less than 6.5 in any element (TOEFL iBT, PTE and other equivalents accepted per Nottingham’s English language policy)"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/studywithus/ugstudy/courses/UG/Law-LLB-Hons.html","label":"Nottingham: Law LLB (Hons) (2027 entry)"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"IELTS 6.5 (no less than 6.5 in any element)"},
