    "us-cs-stanford": {
      "satAct": {"status":"verified","items":["ACT or SAT required — first-year applicants","No minimum test scores; scores are self-reported in the application (official scores required only on enrolment)"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/testing.html","label":"Stanford: Standardized Testing (first-year)"},{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/international/index.html","label":"Stanford: International Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["ACT or SAT scores are required. … There are no minimum test scores required to be admitted to Stanford, and there is no score that guarantees admission.","Yes, the ACT or SAT is required."],"note":"Stanford’s testing page notes ACT/SAT scores were optional for the Class of 2029; the current page (updated July 2026) states they are required. Stanford publishes middle-50% scores of the Class of 2029, which are not requirements. Stanford’s first-year requirements apply to all applicants, whatever the intended major."},
      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["No English proficiency exam required; applicants may self-report scores from any English proficiency exam","Fluency in English is a prerequisite for admission","English proficiency tests cannot substitute for the ACT/SAT requirement"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/international/index.html","label":"Stanford: International Applicants"},{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/testing.html","label":"Stanford: Standardized Testing (first-year)"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["No, we do not require any English proficiency exams. If you would like to send us one, you are welcome to self-report your scores from any English proficiency exam. … Please note that fluency in English is a prerequisite for admission to Stanford.","English Proficiency tests cannot be used as a substitute for the ACT/SAT requirement."]},
      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/index.html","label":"Stanford: First-Year Requirements and Deadlines"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Required Application Components Common Application $100 nonrefundable application fee or fee waiver request ACT or SAT test scores School Report form and counselor letter of recommendation","note":"No course-specific admissions test; the required tests are the ACT or SAT, for all first-year applicants."},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/prepare.html","label":"Stanford: Preparing for Stanford Academics"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"We do not have a set of required courses for admission to Stanford. … Mathematics: four years of rigorous mathematics, including calculus. … We want to emphasize that these are curriculum recommendations, not requirements.","note":"Official: Stanford has no required courses for admission. Its recommended high-school curriculum (stated as recommendations, not requirements) is English four years; mathematics four years, including calculus; history/social studies at least three years; science at least three years; world language at least three years of the same language. Applies to all applicants, not major-specific.","reviewFlag":"Official source lists a recommended high-school curriculum (incl. four years of math including calculus, three+ years of science); data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"Students in the British education system are required to have a school official send GCSE results and predicted A-Level marks for consideration. Stanford says applicants from this system generally will have taken at least three full A-Level courses; it has no preference for a specific curriculum.","sources":[{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/testing.html","label":"Stanford: Standardized Testing (first-year)"},{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/international/index.html","label":"Stanford: International Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Students currently enrolled in the British education system are required to have a school official send us their GCSE results and predicted A-Level marks for consideration. Generally, students applying to Stanford from the British education system will have taken at least three full A-Level courses (though they may not yet have taken the final examinations).","We do not have a preference for a specific curriculum (A-Level, IB, AP, National, etc.)."],"note":"Stanford states no A-Level grade requirement and no minimum scores."},
      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"Students enrolled in an IB Diploma programme outside the U.S. are required to have a school official send predicted IB marks (including TOK/essay bonus points). Stanford has no preference for a specific curriculum.","sources":[{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/testing.html","label":"Stanford: Standardized Testing (first-year)"},{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/international/index.html","label":"Stanford: International Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Students currently enrolled in an IB Diploma program outside the U.S. are required to have a school official send us their predicted IB marks (including TOK/essay bonus points).","We do not have a preference for a specific curriculum (A-Level, IB, AP, National, etc.)."],"note":"Stanford states no IB points requirement and no minimum scores."},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["Advanced Placement: AP exams are not mandatory, but all AP scores taken (including self-studied) must be self-reported in the application"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/testing.html","label":"Stanford: Standardized Testing (first-year)"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"AP exams are not mandatory; however, if you have taken any AP exams, even if you self-studied for them, you are required to self-report all your AP scores in your application."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Interview: optional; offered by alumni volunteers depending on availability in your area — the application is complete with or without one","Arts Portfolio (Art Practice, Dance, Music, Theater and Performance Studies): optional","Letters of recommendation from two academic teachers required"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/interview.html","label":"Stanford: Interview"},{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/arts.html","label":"Stanford: Arts Portfolio"},{"url":"https://admission.stanford.edu/apply/first-year/index.html","label":"Stanford: First-Year Requirements and Deadlines"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["If your high school is in an interview area (listed below), you may be offered an interview with a trained Stanford alumni volunteer, depending on availability. Your application will be considered complete with or without an interview.","Students who wish to highlight their extraordinary talent in the fine or performing arts may submit an Optional Arts Portfolio in one of the following areas: Art Practice, Dance, Music, or Theater and Performance Studies.","Letters of recommendation from two academic teachers"]}
    },
