      "aLevel": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"Princeton evaluates A-levels in the context of the programme’s curriculum. The academic record should include achieved external-exam marks; where leaving exams are part of graduation requirements, the school should submit predicted or achieved results as they become available.","sources":[{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/before-you-apply","label":"Princeton: Before You Apply"},{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/international-students","label":"Princeton: International Students"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["We will evaluate the International Baccalaureate (IB), A-levels or another diploma in the context of the program’s curriculum.","Your academic record should include any available internal grades from classes, achieved marks from external exams (for example: IGCSE, British A-Level, International Baccalaureate, national leaving exams such as Std X/Std XII in India) or a combination of both. If leaving exams are a part of the graduation requirements, please ask your school official to submit predicted or achieved results as they become available."],"note":"Princeton states no A-Level grade requirement."},
      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"Princeton evaluates the IB in the context of the programme’s curriculum. The academic record should include achieved external-exam marks; where leaving exams are part of graduation requirements, the school should submit predicted or achieved results as they become available.","sources":[{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/before-you-apply","label":"Princeton: Before You Apply"},{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/international-students","label":"Princeton: International Students"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["We will evaluate the International Baccalaureate (IB), A-levels or another diploma in the context of the program’s curriculum.","Your academic record should include any available internal grades from classes, achieved marks from external exams (for example: IGCSE, British A-Level, International Baccalaureate, national leaving exams such as Std X/Std XII in India) or a combination of both. If leaving exams are a part of the graduation requirements, please ask your school official to submit predicted or achieved results as they become available."],"note":"Princeton states no IB points requirement. Princeton recommends self-reporting all IB test scores on the application."},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["Advanced Placement: Princeton recommends self-reporting all AP (and IB) test scores on the application"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/standardized-testing","label":"Princeton: Standardized Testing"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If you sat for an Advanced Placement (AP) or International Baccalaureate (IB) test, we recommend that you self-report all of your AP or IB scores on your application.","note":"Princeton’s advanced placement policy (course placement/credit after enrolling) is not an admission requirement and is not recorded here."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Graded written paper required — from an English, social studies or history course in the last three years of secondary school","Princeton-specific Questions required","Alumni interview: optional, subject to alumni availability; opting out is not a disadvantage","Arts Supplement: optional"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/graded-written-paper","label":"Princeton: Graded Written Paper"},{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/application-checklist","label":"Princeton: First-Year Application Checklist"},{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/application-checklist","label":"Princeton: First-Year Application Checklist"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["We ask all students to submit a graded written paper for consideration as part of their application to Princeton. … The paper should be from an academic course in English, social studies or history, from the last three years of secondary school, including senior year.","Princeton-specific Questions. In addition to the questions provided by the Common Application, all applicants must submit the Princeton-specific Questions. … Graded Written Paper. A graded written paper is required, preferably in the subjects of English or history.","Interview. Princeton offers optional alumni interviews. … Arts Supplement, if applicable. If you've excelled in architecture, creative writing, dance, music, music theater, theater or visual arts, and would like us to consider your talent, you are welcome to submit an optional Arts Supplement."]}
