      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["TOEFL, IELTS or Duolingo English Test required for international students for whom English is a second language (exemptions case by case)","University-wide minimum scores: Duolingo 125, IELTS Academic 6.5, TOEFL iBT 5.0 (new scale)","From fall 2027 admission, SAT/ACT scores no longer replace an English test"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.washu.edu/how-to-apply/english-testing-requirements/","label":"WashU: English Testing Requirements"},{"url":"https://oiss.washu.edu/english-proficiency-requirements/","label":"WashU OISS: English Language Proficiency"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["International students for whom English is a second language are required to submit the TOEFL (Test of English as a Foreign Language), IELTS (International English Language Testing System), or Duolingo English Test. … While any students with scores above these minimums are welcome to apply, our most competitive undergraduate applicants share scores in the following ranges or above: … Beginning with students applying for Fall 2027 admission, SAT or ACT scores will no longer be accepted in lieu of English proficiency exam scores.","WashU accepted tests and minimum score requirements: Duolingo English Test (DET) – 125 minimum overall score … International English Language Testing System (IELTS) Academic – 6.5 minimum composite score Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL) iBT – 5.0 overall (new scale) OR 4.5 ≥ 90 overall (old scale)"],"note":"The minimums are WashU’s university-wide English proficiency minimums (Office for International Students & Scholars), linked from the admissions page; the old-scale TOEFL figure is printed unclearly there (“4.5 ≥ 90”). WashU admissions also publishes scores of its most competitive applicants (TOEFL 100 / 5.0, IELTS 7.0, Duolingo 130), not minimum scores, so those are not shown as requirements."},
      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.washu.edu/how-to-apply/first-year-us-applicants/","label":"WashU: First-Year U.S. Citizen/Permanent Resident Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Counselor recommendation and one teacher evaluation A 250-word response to the question “Please tell us what you are interested in studying at college and why.” Extracurricular and community activities The Common Application or Coalition Application essay"},
