      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["No direct first-year entry to the B.S. in Commerce: students apply to McIntire in the spring of their first year at UVA and, if accepted, start in their second year","Prerequisites to apply: COMM 1800 Foundations of Commerce, ECON 2010 Principles of Microeconomics, and the First Writing Requirement (taken at UVA)","Applicants with college credit from high school still complete at least one academic year at UVA first"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.commerce.virginia.edu/bs-commerce/admissions/first-years","label":"UVA McIntire: First-Year Student Admissions Process and Requirements"},{"url":"https://www.commerce.virginia.edu/bs-commerce/admissions/first-years","label":"UVA McIntire: First-Year Student Admissions Process and Requirements"},{"url":"https://www.commerce.virginia.edu/bs-commerce/admissions/first-years","label":"UVA McIntire: First-Year Student Admissions Process and Requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Students who are in their first year can apply to the program in the spring semester of their first year of classes. If accepted, they will start the program in August of their second year.","Students must complete the following prerequisite courses, including the First Writing Requirement, to apply to McIntire: … COMM 1800: Foundations of Commerce (3 credits) … ECON 2010: Principles of Microeconomics (3 credits)","High school students who have enough credits and have completed college-level prerequisite courses still need to complete a minimum of one academic year at UVA before enrollment at McIntire."],"note":"This covers McIntire’s internal application only. UVA’s first-year application requirements (essays, supplements) could not be checked because admission.virginia.edu returned 403 (Cloudflare bot challenge) on 2026-10-19."}
