      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["International applicants whose first language is not English are evaluated for English proficiency; an exam is the most common and preferred evidence","Required minimum: TOEFL iBT 4.5 with at least 4.0 per section (88 with 20 per section for tests before 21 Jan 2026); ACT English 26 or SAT EBRW 600 also qualify","Scores must be from a test taken within the past two years"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.purdue.edu/become-student/english-proficiency/","label":"Purdue: English Proficiency"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"International undergraduate applicants whose first language is not English will be evaluated for English language proficiency during the application review process. … The most common and preferred way to provide evidence of English language proficiency is through an exam. … We require a minimum TOEFL iBT score of 4.5 or higher with at least a 4.0 in each section. … We require a minimum TOEFL iBT score of 88 or higher with at least a 20 or higher per section. … You must have a score of 26 or higher on the English section. … You must have a score of 600 or better on the Evidence-based Reading and Writing (EBRW) section. … Score results must be from a test taken within the past two years.","note":"For the Duolingo English Test (115, subscores 110) and IELTS (6.5, 6.0 per section) Purdue states what applicants “generally” have, not a minimum, so those figures are not shown as requirements. A completed English-taught curriculum (at least three years, B or better in English) may also be considered."},
      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.purdue.edu/become-student/guide/","label":"Purdue: Your Guide to Applying"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"For most first-year students, a complete application includes: … The application itself (including an essay) … Answers to Purdue-specific questions on the application … Self-reported high school grades … Self-reported ACT or SAT scores","note":"No course-specific admissions test is listed for this major."},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.purdue.edu/majors/computer-science/","label":"Purdue: Computer Science"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Minimum high school coursework (many applicants exceed these minimums): … Math – 4 years … English – 4 years … Lab science – 3 years … Social studies – 3 years … World language – 2 years","note":"Official: minimum high-school coursework — Math 4 years, English 4 years, Lab science 3 years, Social studies 3 years, World language 2 years (can be different languages); may also be met through nonremedial college-level coursework.","reviewFlag":"Official source lists minimum high-school coursework (Math 4, English 4, Lab science 3, Social studies 3, World language 2 years); data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"No AS- or A-Level subject requirements. Applicants who do not study beyond IGCSE/GCSE are generally not considered competitive. IGCSE/GCSE applicants need passes in at least five academic subjects including English, mathematics, a natural/physical science and a social science.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.purdue.edu/become-student/international/","label":"Purdue: International Students"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Purdue does not have any AS- or A-level subject requirements; however, most applicants complete three to four AS- or A-level subjects. Applicants that do not complete any further study beyond IGCSE or GCSE are generally not considered competitive applicants. … you are required to have passed examinations in a minimum of five academic subjects including English, mathematics, natural/physical science and social science.","note":"Purdue says most applicants complete three to four AS- or A-level subjects — a description of applicants, not a requirement. No A-Level grade offer is stated."},
      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"IB students are considered with or without the full IB Diploma, provided the minimum high-school course requirements are met; HL is not preferred over SL; no overall IB minimum score; submit predicted IB scores if available.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.purdue.edu/become-student/international/","label":"Purdue: International Students"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If you are taking International Baccalaureate (IB) courses, you will be considered for admission whether or not you are pursuing the IB diploma as long as the minimum high school course requirements are met. For admission purposes, higher level (HL) coursework is not given a particular preference over standard level (SL) coursework. … Purdue does not have an overall IB minimum score requirement. … Predicted IB scores if available"},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"partial","items":["CLT scores are accepted alongside SAT/ACT","Purdue advises taking available AP, IB or dual-enrollment courses"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.purdue.edu/become-student/guide/","label":"Purdue: Your Guide to Applying"},{"url":"https://admissions.purdue.edu/become-student/course-requirements/","label":"Purdue: High School Course Requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["We accept SAT, ACT or CLT scores and have no preference on which test you take.","Take advantage of any available Advanced Placement (AP), International Baccalaureate (IB) or dual enrollment courses."],"note":"Purdue’s admissions pages checked (guide, first-year criteria, course requirements, international) do not say whether AP exam scores are used or can be self-reported for admission; AP/A-Level credit pages are about credit after enrolling."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Common App essay plus Purdue’s required questions (250 words or fewer each), including why you chose your major"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.purdue.edu/become-student/guide/","label":"Purdue: Your Guide to Applying"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Your application will include both a Common App essay and response to Purdue’s required questions. … Respond in 250 words or fewer to each of these required questions."}
